#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:3
msgid "Security"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:5
msgid ""
"Microsoft takes the security of our software products and services "
"seriously, which includes all source code repositories managed through "
"our GitHub organizations, which include "
"[Microsoft](https://github.com/Microsoft), "
"[Azure](https://github.com/Azure), [DotNet](https://github.com/dotnet), "
"[AspNet](https://github.com/aspnet), "
"[Xamarin](https://github.com/xamarin), and [our GitHub "
"organizations](https://opensource.microsoft.com/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:7
msgid ""
"If you believe you have found a security vulnerability in any Microsoft-"
"owned repository that meets [Microsoft's definition of a security "
"vulnerability](https://aka.ms/opensource/security/definition), please "
"report it to us as described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:9
msgid "Reporting Security Issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:11
msgid ""
"**Please do not report security vulnerabilities through public GitHub "
"issues.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:13
msgid ""
"Instead, please report them to the Microsoft Security Response Center "
"(MSRC) at [https://msrc.microsoft.com/create-"
"report](https://aka.ms/opensource/security/create-report)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:15
msgid ""
"If you prefer to submit without logging in, send email to "
"[secure@microsoft.com](mailto:secure@microsoft.com).  If possible, "
"encrypt your message with our PGP key; please download it from the "
"[Microsoft Security Response Center PGP Key "
"page](https://aka.ms/opensource/security/pgpkey)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:17
msgid ""
"You should receive a response within 24 hours. If for some reason you do "
"not, please follow up via email to ensure we received your original "
"message. Additional information can be found at "
"[microsoft.com/msrc](https://aka.ms/opensource/security/msrc)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:19
msgid ""
"Please include the requested information listed below (as much as you can"
" provide) to help us better understand the nature and scope of the "
"possible issue:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:21
msgid ""
"Type of issue (e.g. buffer overflow, SQL injection, cross-site scripting,"
" etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:22
msgid "Full paths of source file(s) related to the manifestation of the issue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:23
msgid "The location of the affected source code (tag/branch/commit or direct URL)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:24
msgid "Any special configuration required to reproduce the issue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:25
msgid "Step-by-step instructions to reproduce the issue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:26
msgid "Proof-of-concept or exploit code (if possible)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:27
msgid "Impact of the issue, including how an attacker might exploit the issue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:29
msgid "This information will help us triage your report more quickly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:31
msgid ""
"If you are reporting for a bug bounty, more complete reports can "
"contribute to a higher bounty award. Please visit our [Microsoft Bug "
"Bounty Program](https://aka.ms/opensource/security/bounty) page for more "
"details about our active programs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:33
msgid "Preferred Languages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:35
msgid "We prefer all communications to be in English."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:37
msgid "Policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/tslib_SECURITY.md:39
msgid ""
"Microsoft follows the principle of [Coordinated Vulnerability "
"Disclosure](https://aka.ms/opensource/security/cvd)."
msgstr ""

